    <!--
        This comment must sit INSIDE the root element. A comment placed ABOVE <PermissionSet>
        breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with the misleading error "unable to find matching
        parent xml file". Broker_Protection_Access is the precedent for this pattern.

        NDA__c CARRIES viewAllRecords=true, AND THAT IS AN ACCEPTED, INFORMED WIDENING - NOT
        DRIFT, AND NOT SOMETHING TO TIDY AWAY (user decision 2026-08-09, decisions file D12/W3;
        raised as code review W3).

        Gate 1 Q7 specified a plain allowRead on NDA__c plus FLS on Status__c, so that the BOV
        Outreach tile could report real NDA status instead of a hard-coded value. What shipped
        is allowRead PLUS viewAllRecords, mirroring DPEG_Acquisition_View.

        WHY THE PLAIN READ WOULD HAVE BEEN WRONG: NDA__c is sharingModel Private with no
        relevant sharing rule, and one NDA__c object serves BOTH the acquisition and the
        disposition module. A disposition user with a plain read therefore sees only the NDA
        rows shared to them - which for most rows is none - so the pill would report "No NDA"
        for an NDA THAT EXISTS AND IS SIGNED. That is a false compliance negative: the tile
        would LIE BY OMISSION, which is the exact defect this grant was added to fix, and it is
        strictly worse than the hard-coded value it replaced because it looks authoritative.

        WHAT IT COSTS, STATED PLAINLY: a disposition-only persona can now read EVERY NDA in the
        org, including acquisition NDAs, in a security model the 2026-07-22 RBAC build
        deliberately partitioned by module. Read-only; no create, edit or delete on NDA__c.

        THE CORRECT LONG-TERM SHAPE IS view-all SCOPED TO DISPOSITION NDAs. That is not
        expressible today: it needs record types on NDA__c, which Tranche 3 (decision D7) adds.
        REVISIT THEN - and only then. Narrowing this to a plain read before those record types
        exist re-opens the lying pill; the same comment is on DPEG_Disposition_Edit and both
        must move together.

        ================================================================================
        SUPERSEDED 2026-08-09 BY DECISION D17. viewAllRecords ON NDA__c IS NOW FALSE.
        The block above is KEPT AS HISTORY. It no longer describes the grant.
        ================================================================================

        WHAT D17 DOES HERE: viewAllRecords on NDA__c drops to FALSE. allowRead stays true;
        allowCreate, allowEdit and allowDelete stay false - this is the READ-ONLY Principal
        persona and its CRUD is untouched. Record visibility now comes from CRITERIA-BASED
        SHARING RULES on NDA__c scoped to RecordTypeId = NDA__c.Disposition_NDA - see
        sharingRules/NDA__c.sharingRules-meta.xml.

        WHY THIS SUPERSEDES RATHER THAN CONTRADICTS THE TEXT ABOVE: that text did not argue
        org-wide visibility was desirable. It said the correct shape - view-all SCOPED TO
        DISPOSITION NDAs - "is not expressible today: it needs record types on NDA__c, which
        Tranche 3 (decision D7) adds. REVISIT THEN." THE RECORD TYPES NOW EXIST. D17 is that
        revisit. The org-wide grant existed only because the scoping mechanism did not.

        🔴 THIS SET IS THE REASON THE SECOND SHARING RULE EXISTS. This is the persona held by
        the PRINCIPALS via DPEG_Principal_PSG, and principals are not necessarily members of
        DPEG_Acquisitions_Team - the group every other disposition child object shares to. With
        viewAllRecords gone and only a team rule in place, principals would have silently lost
        NDA visibility entirely, and the BOV Outreach pill would report "No NDA" for NDAs that
        exist - the exact defect the D12/W3 text above was written to prevent. The rule
        NDA_Disposition_Principals_R shares Disposition_NDA rows to the Principals group at
        Read, which is the strictly lower access this persona needs.

        🔴 GROUP MEMBERSHIP IS ORG STATE AND IS NOT DEPLOYABLE. If the Principals group is empty
        or wrong after deploy, this persona sees no NDAs at all. Post-deploy gate.

        🔴 DEPLOY SHARING RULES ONE AT A TIME - a batch rolls all of them back in this org.

        NOTE the two files still move together on viewAllRecords, as the text above requires -
        both went to false in the same change. They DIVERGE on CRUD only: D16.1 gave
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit allowEdit=true and deliberately left this set read-only.
    -->
    <!--
