    <!--
        AMENDED 2026-08-09 BY DECISION D24 - PSA_Version__c: viewAllRecords FALSE to TRUE. Object
        read stays READ ONLY (allowCreate, allowEdit and allowDelete were already false on this
        set and are untouched). The full reasoning lives in the matching D24 block on
        DPEG_Disposition_Edit; only what is DIFFERENT for THIS persona is written here.

        This SUPERSEDES the "🔴 PSA_Version__c HAS NO SHARING RULE AND THIS PERSONA IS THE
        SHARPEST CASE" section of the D23 block above, and its header line "🔴 NO
        viewAllRecords", both KEPT AS HISTORY. That section said the three closure options were a
        user decision, as at D21. The user has picked option (a).

        WHAT THIS GRANTS, WITHOUT SOFTENING: a Principal can now READ EVERY PSA VERSION IN THE
        ORG, acquisition rows included - the full redline history of every live PURCHASE, which
        terms DPEG conceded and in what order. Informed widening of the same class as NDA__c at
        D12/W3 and Counter_Offer__c at D21.

        WHY THIS SET IS THE SHARPEST CASE, AND WHY A LOOKUP CHILD LEFT NO OTHER OPTION TODAY.
        PSA_Version__c's parent field is a LOOKUP, not a master detail, and the object is Private
        OWD, so it does NOT inherit the Contract_Review__c scoping this tranche ships; the parent
        rules reach the parent and stop. A PRINCIPAL CREATES NOTHING, so unlike the Edit persona
        they do not even see rows by ownership: with no rule they saw ZERO versions. 🔴 AND THE
        FAILURE IS SILENT - an unshared row is FILTERED OUT of a WITH USER_MODE query rather than
        refused, so the version history renders EMPTY and an approver cannot tell that apart from
        a PSA with no redline rounds. That is precisely the failure
        Contract_Review_Disp_Principals_R exists to prevent on the parent, one object further
        down.

        THE TWO ALTERNATIVES REJECTED (stated here too, because this file is read on its own):
        MASTER DETAIL conversion would make the object ControlledByParent and need no field, no
        Apex and no rule, but it FORCES CASCADE DELETE - deleting a Contract Review would destroy
        its whole version history, the opposite of the allowDelete=false discipline. A STORED
        DISCRIMINATOR checkbox plus a criteria rule is the narrow long term shape, but it is a
        FIELD plus APEX plus a BACKFILL of existing rows, not a sharing change. A criteria rule on
        today's schema was never available: no record types, and Direction__c means the
        counterparty on BOTH sides.

        🔴 THE COUNTER CORRUPTION IS FIXED IN APEX, NOT HERE. The D23 block above reports that
        PsaVersionSelector's `SELECT COUNT()` is WITH USER_MODE and PsaVersionService writes
        `priorCount + 1` into Latest_Version__c, so a user who could not see the priors counted
        zero and rewound the counter to 1. That is being closed in a separate Apex change (the
        count moves to WITH SYSTEM_MODE under the ARCHITECTURE.md §2 automation path exception,
        computing a DERIVED FIELD rather than serving a human's read; 3B
        LoiSelector.selectNegotiationContextById precedent). THIS GRANT IS NOT THAT FIX. It masks
        the symptom for this persona only while it is in force, so do not treat the Apex change as
        redundant and do not re solve the counter with permissions - the next persona without the
        grant would corrupt the data rather than merely fail to read it.

        NO recordTypeVisibilities ARE ADDED. PSA_Version__c has no record types; that is also why
        no criteria rule was expressible for it.

        🔴 A PermissionSet DEPLOY REPLACES THIS SET'S ENTIRE GRANT LIST. The reconciliation
        recorded in the D21 block above (retrieve of 2026-08-09, no org only grants) is CITED, NOT
        RE RUN, for this edit. Re run the retrieve and the diff immediately before deploying.
        🔴 No sharing rule is shipped for PSA_Version__c by this decision and none is pending;
        view all covers it on both disposition sets. The D23 Contract_Review__c rules are
        unchanged and still deploy ONE AT A TIME. Verify AS THE PERSONA, never as an
        administrator.
    -->
